      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:3:4:20:17",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/4/18/17",
      "text": [
        " لاِمْرَأَتِهِ أَنْتِ عَلَيَّ كَظَهْرِ أُمِّي مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ، فَقَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ \"يُطِيقُ لِكُلِّ مَرَّةٍ عِتْقَ نَسَمَةٍ\" فَقَالَ لاَ قَالَ \"يُطِيقُ إِطْعَامَ \"سِتِّينَ مِسْكِيناً\" مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ\" قَالَ لاَ قَالَ \"فَيُطِيقُ صِيَامَ \"شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتٰابِعَيْنِ\" مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ\" قَالَ لاَ قَالَ \"يُفَرَّقُ بَيْنَهُمَا \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4842 - Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir narrated from Abu al-Ward that Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) was asked, while I was present, about a man who said to his wife, \"You are to me like the back of my mother\" a hundred times.\nAbu Jafar Imam Al-Baqir (as) said: \"Is he able to free a slave for each time?\"\nThe man replied: \"No.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Is he able to feed sixty needy people for each time?\"\nThe man replied: \"No.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Is he able to fast for two consecutive months for each time?\"\nThe man replied: \"No.\"\nImam (as) then said: \"They should be separated.\""
        ]
      }
    },
